{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T03:31:49.948Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6a627c6a9d6772d54597ee42","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2nwcgg","claim:pm-dhlij3","claim:pm-x9r2h3","lineage:pm-2nwcgg","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-2nwcgg+pm-dhlij3+pm-x9r2h3","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2nwcgg","claim:pm-dhlij3","claim:pm-x9r2h3","lineage:pm-2nwcgg","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T03:31:49.948Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-27T03:31:49.947Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Fix (2026-11-27, branch fix/field-admission-diagnostics). The registry's per-definition normalizer is now inspectRuntimeFieldDefinition in src/core/schema/runtime-schema.ts: it returns the resolved definition plus a loss record (dropped: not_an_object | key_empty | cli_flag_empty | value_schema_invalid; ignored: one line per member it skips). normalizeRuntimeFieldDefinition reads it, so the diagnostic cannot disagree with the registry. pm validate --check-metadata calls scanFieldDefinitionLosses (src/sdk/schema/field-definition-losses.ts), which reads the stored entries themselves, inline in settings.json and in the configured fields file, and reports rows {source, index, key, dropped|ignored} with validate_schema_field_definition_dropped:<n> and validate_schema_field_definition_partial:<n>. Ignored members covered: blank or non-string aliases, aliases that are not a list, an unknown or non-string type (read as string), unknown commands, blank required_types, a non-string description, and an explicit metadata_key or front_matter_key that names nothing. Two defects found while probing the dropped shapes, fixed here: a null entry in schema/fields.json, statuses.json or types.json threw inside the normalizers, so readSettings failed its merge and every setting fell back to its default (settings_read_merge_failed); entries that are not objects are now skipped with runtime_schema_<section>_entry_invalid:<n>, which health reports. And a description that is not a string threw the same way. Second: a metadata_key that normalizes to nothing stored every value under the empty item key (the item file held a line with an empty key); it now falls back to the field key and validate reports it. Negative control on the published 2026.11.26 build: validate --check-metadata reports nothing for the same fields file and the null entry yields settings_read_merge_failed. Spec: tests/unit/sdk/schema/field-definition-losses.spec.ts (21 cases, including registry parity for every shape)."}]}],"before_hash":"1224e96f7e27f5fff26a727ea0887f4665e3c442fa7099f8884dfcef9cea0c8d","after_hash":"277224d1163e7f8c0d0d980bf6359fcd6578dad16d76104b23676a9da8cdfbf7","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"fa2e6bbb7561179fbc297ca9751dd90e9b66c348b86192e9aec77bda57e2f439"}
