{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T04:28:32.402Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6a627c6a9d6772d54597ee42","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-27T04:28:32.402Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 1 (gpt-6.2-sol xhigh, 2026-11-27) on e02d401c0: 7 findings on this item, all verified and fixed. (1) A null metadata_key no longer hides front_matter_key: the explicit key keeps the nullish precedence the old normalizer used. (2) An unreadable fields file (a directory) no longer crashes validate: readStoredJson catches read errors, and the inline rows still report. (3) Inline entries are judged as settings validation admits them: validation strips an inline value_schema (the field registers, so no row is due) and refuses a document with an unknown inline type (the settings read replaces it with defaults and reports it), so the scan reads validateSettings(...).data. (4) The registry normalizes a definition more than once, and stripFlagPrefix removed one dash pair per pass, so cli_flag '----' passed the single-pass inspection but was dropped by the registry; stripFlagPrefix now removes every leading pair in one pass, which matches the registry's final result and makes normalization idempotent. (5) Non-boolean repeatable, required, required_on_create and allow_unset values are reported with the behavior they leave in place. (6) Diagnostic formatting never throws (a BigInt or cyclic alias used to throw from JSON.stringify, which would have changed whether the field resolves). (7) The fix hint says add-field keeps a stored value_schema, so value_schema_invalid needs an edit of the file. Specs added in field-definition-losses.spec.ts (30 cases, 100% of the module)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T04:28:32.402Z"}],"before_hash":"f25633659ca457f336368f5eecaed8f3c9bcff90f8d03b7aa6d426ce4abf824b","after_hash":"dd01155c8b409ac325d52fc9052f22a83ccf783f88e1bcea5b0a3ee8f9814849","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"61f3b0b3c54e722079eb5c41120d5e415abae8f0d530e27aeb3d4b92c3ed3f03"}
